  <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-inner">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">Last updated: July 27, 2025</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="legal-inner">

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll">
        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          ShortDesk ("we", "us", "our") is an open-source URL shortening service.
          This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect information
          when you use our service at shortdesk.app and any self-hosted instances.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.05s">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <h3>2.1 URLs You Submit</h3>
        <p>
          When you create a shortened link, we store the original URL, a generated
          short code, and any optional metadata you provide (custom alias, password hash,
          expiry date, webhook URL).
        </p>
        <h3>2.2 Click Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          When someone clicks a shortened link, we collect anonymous data including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>IP address (used to determine country, not stored long-term)</li>
          <li>User-Agent string (parsed into device, browser, OS)</li>
          <li>Referrer header</li>
          <li>Timestamp of the click</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.3 No Account Data</h3>
        <p>
          ShortDesk does not require user accounts. We do not collect names, email
          addresses, or passwords for authentication purposes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.1s">
        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We use collected data solely to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Redirect short URLs to their original destination</li>
          <li>Provide click analytics to link creators</li>
          <li>Enforce password protection and expiry rules</li>
          <li>Send webhook notifications when thresholds are reached</li>
          <li>Check URLs against Google Safe Browsing for security</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.15s">
        <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Shortened links and their analytics are stored indefinitely unless:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The link has an expiry date set by the creator</li>
          <li>The link creator requests deletion</li>
          <li>A self-hosted instance has its own retention policies</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.2s">
        <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>We use the following third-party services:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Safe Browsing API</strong> — to check submitted URLs for known threats. No personal data is sent.</li>
          <li><strong>QR Code Generation</strong> — done server-side, no external API calls.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell, share, or transfer any data to third parties for advertising
          or marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.25s">
        <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          ShortDesk uses a single session cookie for password-protected links.
          This cookie is set only when you access a protected link and enter the
          correct password. It contains no personal data and expires after 24 hours.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also use <code>localStorage</code> to remember your theme preference
          (dark/light mode). This data never leaves your browser.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.3s">
        <h2>7. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take security seriously:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt before storage</li>
          <li>All URLs are checked against Google Safe Browsing</li>
          <li>Rate limiting is applied to prevent abuse</li>
          <li>The source code is open for public audit</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.35s">
        <h2>8. Self-Hosted Instances</h2>
        <p>
          ShortDesk is open source and can be self-hosted. If you deploy your own
          instance, you are the data controller and are responsible for your own
          privacy compliance. This policy applies only to the official hosted version.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.4s">
        <h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request deletion of links you created</li>
          <li>Request a copy of analytics data for your links</li>
          <li>Contact us with any privacy concerns</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.45s">
        <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this
          page with an updated revision date. Continued use of the service after changes
          constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-card reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.5s">
        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy-related questions, open an issue on
          <a href="https://github.com/aminilay/shortdesk-official/issues" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
          or contact the maintainer at
          <a href="https://github.com/aminilay" target="_blank">github.com/aminilay</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-nav-buttons reveal-scroll" style="--reveal-delay:0.55s">
        <a href="/terms" class="btn btn-ghost">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-ghost">Documentation</a>
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Back to Home</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
<footer class="landing-footer">
  <div class="footer-inner">
    <div class="footer-col footer-brand-col">
      <div class="footer-logo">
        <img src="/assets/dm.png" alt="ShortDesk" class="footer-logo-img logo-dark">
        <img src="/assets/lm.png" alt="ShortDesk" class="footer-logo-img logo-light">
        <span class="footer-brand">ShortDesk</span>
      </div>
      <p class="footer-tagline">Smart, trackable, password-protected short links. Open source and free forever.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-col">
      <h4 class="footer-col-title">Product</h4>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a href="/#features">Features</a>
      <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
      <a href="/">Create Link</a>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-col">
      <h4 class="footer-col-title">Resources</h4>
      <a href="/docs">Documentation</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/aminilay/shortdesk-official" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/aminilay/shortdesk-official/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank">License (MIT)</a>
